// Title: Add SafeBoot Keys Via Reg Utility
// Sigma ID: d7662ff6-9e97-4596-a61d-9839e32dee8d
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-09-02 | Modified: 2024-03-19
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1685
// Description: Detects execution of "reg.exe" commands with the "add" or "copy" flags on safe boot registry
//   keys. Often used by attacker to allow the ransomware to work in safe mode as some security
//   products do not
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://redacted.com/blog/bianlian-ransomware-gang-gives-it-a-go/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_reg_add_safeboot.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\reg.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "reg.exe") and ProcessCommandLine contains "\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SafeBoot" and (ProcessCommandLine contains " copy " or ProcessCommandLine contains " add ")
